First-event score gap 0. Truncated-prefix replay error 0.
\image(figures/temporal_graph_fit.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Held-out link loss and positive-link ranking after four warm-up events on each stream.)
\alttext(Two line plots of held-out suffix loss and the fraction of events whose positive link ranks higher than the sampled negative.)

At the first event both candidates have zero memory and the scores agree.
The prefix check confirms that future events do not affect earlier scores.

> Reference

- [Rossi et al. (2020), Temporal Graph Networks for Deep Learning on Dynamic Graphs](https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.10637).
